{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Change 3401 patchset 1 got Verified -1 (CI run 43543141368): the pip-audit dependency-advisory gate reported CVE-2026-126360 (unrated, treated HIGH) in opentelemetry-api 1.45.1, fix 1.45.2. Per docs/dependency-advisory-runbook.md §1 the finding belongs to this change because it edits uv.lock (the version bump). `uv lock --upgrade-package opentelemetry-api` alone was a no-op because opentelemetry-sdk pins the API exactly, so the whole OTel family (10 packages) moved together to 1.45.2 / 0.66b2. `scripts/dependency_audit.py gate --lane gerrit` on the new lock: \"pip-audit: OK (no known vulnerabilities)\". Re-running make verify before the patchset 2 push. uv.lock is not part of the wheel, so the published package is unaffected."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1794622774861929278,"uuid":"0047dc26-ecf3-478e-88a5-17ae7cef88ad"}